/**
 * Concise, executable guidance advertised in DevSpace MCP tool metadata.
 * Keep action signatures in sync with the corresponding Zod input schemas.
 * Full recipes: tips/AGENT_TOOL_USE.md in this repository.
 */
export const TIP_TOOL_DESCRIPTIONS=Object.freeze({
  tips_project: `Project-wide Tips research overview, from the SAME durable task cards (no duplicate backlog). Projects: air (AIR-LIFE, AIR / Paper, AIR-Research, AIR / Other and related Subs), infrastructure, other. overview/list: status totals, workstreams and prioritized tasks; get/history inspect task ID. Ordinary authenticated agents can create a NEW task with stable id, projectId, title, message and optional nextAction/acceptanceCriteria/priority, but cannot overwrite a plan. edit/archive/delete require either a genuinely authenticated claimed Web Main identity (web-main or web-*-main), or the private Tips viewToken; claimed Web Sub cannot manage. edit can change owner, nextAction, acceptanceCriteria, priority, gate, status; expectedUpdatedAt prevents stale edits. Archive first; only archived non-running tasks may be deleted. Operations are audited. Normal worker progress can still be reported via tips(action=update) on the same task. Never confuse editing the project plan with permission to override STOP/GPU/Owner/dispatch_hold.`,
  tips_skills: `Read-only optional Agent skills. Use tips_skills({action:"list"}), then tips_skills({action:"read",name:"project-overview"}) for authoritative AIR project/task CRUD and manager permissions. Other skills: agent-coordination (Web/Local Main/Sub, Sol/Luna), main-batch-triage (coalesced Sol mailbox), research-safety (GPU/STOP/Owner), tips-troubleshooting (Web Wake and ACK). Local Codex can read the same $CODEX_HOME/skills/<name>/SKILL.md. No model execution, messages, secrets or arbitrary files. Only read relevant Skill; do not inject manuals every turn.`,
  tips_admin: `Privileged maintenance for the Tips research console and Agent registry. Use the SAME private Tips viewToken as /tips; no separate admin key. Every MCP call needs viewToken (web UI reuses its already authenticated Bearer view token automatically). Example: tips_admin({action:"remove_web",id:"web-old",viewToken:"PRIVATE_TIPS_VIEW_TOKEN",reason:"retired"}). Actions: history (recent management audit, no id), revoke_web (invalidate Web claim, keep role slot), remove_web (remove Web registration and invalidate claim, preserve historical mail), stop_sub (request orderly stop), remove_sub (only for stopped/completed/failed Sub; archives Codex thread pointer), reset_sub_failure (requires actual diagnosis in reason; does NOT retry), archive_task and delete_task (nonrunning tasks only), delete_message (not while processing). Never delete running Local Sub registration or an in-process request. Main and tmux are observed processes, not removable registrations. Every mutation is audited, but the view token is never logged. Treat the view token as a full-management secret, not a public read-only token.`,
  tips: `Tips task progress board at /tips (NOT an agent mailbox).
Actions: list (default), get {id}, update {id,title?,status?,kind?,message?,details?,group?,...}, heartbeat {id}, history {id,limit?}. Use tips_project for project-wide overview, create and manager-curated edit/archive/delete; ordinary tips users cannot delete/archive a task directly.
Example: tips({action:"update",id:"air-review-01",title:"CPU-only audit",status:"running",kind:"text",group:"AIR",message:"Checking prerequisites"}). Keep a stable task ID and post truthful status changes; use heartbeatEnabled=true plus repeated heartbeat for ongoing jobs (default stale timeout 300s). Task progress 100% is not proof an experiment succeeded. Statuses blocked/paused/cancelled are distinct. This tool updates shared server-side Tips history; it does NOT execute research or send a message. For communication use tips_messages (server Agents) or web_mail (claimed Web Chats).`,

  tips_messages: `Durable Tips mailbox for Local Agents. Claimed web-* sender identities MUST use web_mail to avoid impersonation. Trusted post/reply TO server-controller requests a Sol wake unless wake:false explicitly opts out. Normal-priority requests wait 10 minutes to batch progress updates; priority:high and authorized safety gates are immediate. Do not label routine progress high priority. Example: tips_messages({action:"post",from:"sub-foo",to:"server-controller",subject:"Progress checkpoint",body:"Evidence and next decision"}). Plain HTTP write tokens cannot wake Sol. Main triages queued messages in one model Turn rather than one model call per message. Messages addressed to web-* cause Web Wake notifications only when a matching claimed role/browser is online; they do not run cloud inference by themselves. Main-to-web tracked handoffs use tips/web-handoff.mjs request with one 45min/3h fallback. Read: {action:"list",to:"server-controller",unreadOnly:true}; reply: {action:"reply",from:"server-controller",to:"sub-foo",inReplyTo:"MESSAGE_ID",body:"..."}; ACK after actual reading, resolve after actual completion, tracked VERIFY after checking evidence. Never fake delivery/ACK.`,

  tips_exchange: `Tracked Web-controller-to-App-Server-Sub handoff with an immutable message ID and server-side audit events; NOT a ChatGPT conversation log.
Submit: tips_exchange({action:"submit",to:"sub-cpu-review",subject:"Verify CPU evidence",body:"Please audit the log"}) -> accepted/id means QUEUED, not finished. Get: {action:"get",id:"MESSAGE_ID"} returns original message, ACK, recipient verdict and related replies. List: {action:"list",to:"sub-cpu-review",limit:20}. Recipient must read/ACK and explicitly verify accepted|rejected|needs_changes after checking evidence; plain resolve is forbidden for tracked messages. The App Server adapter records verdicts in its <tips-actions> footer. Poll reasonably rather than in tight loops; no promise of immediate model completion. Submit currently only supports a sub-* recipient; to send AS a claimed web-* chat (including tracked messages to other Web Chats), use web_mail(action:"send",tracked:true) instead. Records are visible on /tips; a web chat is not automatically awakened.`,

  subagent: `Manage durable Codex App Server sub-* Agents with Tips messaging; prefer this over launching new long-lived codex exec loops. The registry supports 128 distinct persisted sub-* identities; this does NOT mean 128 concurrent processes: the manager defaults to 2 simultaneous agents and has a hard upper bound of 4. Reuse completed threads with the same name/model/cwd/sandbox whenever suitable. The Tips protocol is injected ONCE per persistent thread; busy managed threads may receive turn/steer with eventual ACK rather than synchronous acceptance.
start: subagent({action:"start",name:"sub-air-cpu",goal:"Audit CPU baseline",cwd:"/absolute/allowed/workspace",model:"gpt-6-luna",sandbox:"workspace-write"}) returns accepted:true and status:queued, NOT completion. A Tips task card with ID equal to the sub-* name is CREATED immediately on queue; use /tips to see pending/running/heartbeat/completion/failure and milestones, no SSH needed. The Local Sub must publish evidence-backed stage updates to its task card using tips-cli update; the manager adds periodic tool-activity snapshots without inventing progress percentages. Each name has an independent persisted Codex Thread. status {name} gives latest state and lastResult; stop {name} requests termination. message {name,from:"server-controller",subject:"Correction",body:"..."} posts trusted durable mail and links to the same Tips task card; active Subs receive steer when supported, idle Subs wake in their original thread. Delivery is not ACK. Default gpt-6-luna; use gpt-6.1-sol only for hard checks. Respect GPU freezes, STOP, preregistration, and Owner locks. Claimed web-* must use web_mail instead of spoofing sender.`,

  web_identity: `Identity registry for EACH separately claimed ChatGPT Web conversation, independent of the shared DevSpace OAuth account.
Step 1 (preparing Chat): web_identity({action:"prepare",id:"web-reviewer-01",label:"Reviewer"}) -> private one-use invite valid 10 minutes. Step 2 (new Chat): {action:"claim",id:"web-reviewer-01",invite:"INVITE"} -> immediate self-claim, NO manual approval. Step 3 (same Chat later): {action:"whoami"} -> recognized identity when the MCP host exposes stable openai/session metadata. If whoami says recognized:false, supply the private claimKey returned at claim; without stable metadata, pass that key on subsequent web_identity/web_mail calls. {action:"list"} shows nonsecret IDs/status; {action:"renew"} extends the 7-day lease; {action:"release"} cancels your own claim. Management cleanup: {action:"revoke",id:"web-old",viewToken:"PRIVATE_TIPS_VIEW_TOKEN"} uses the SAME Tips view key already used on /tips; no second admin key. The old claim is invalidated while preserving past messages. Lease expiration is NOT deletion of role/history. Never post viewToken/invite/claimKey to Tips, project files, or Git.`,

  web_mail: `Identity-bound Web Chat ↔ Web Chat / Server Agent mailbox. First web_identity(claim/whoami); sender is bound to YOUR claimed identity, no from parameter is accepted. send: web_mail({action:"send",to:"server-controller",subject:"AIR review checkpoint",body:"Evidence and question",tracked:true}) requests a Sol wake by default, but routine priority waits 10 minutes to coalesce; genuine priority:high wakes immediately; wake:false stores a passive note. To send to another Web role: {action:"send",to:"web-reviewer-01",tracked:true,subject:"Review",body:"Check results"}. Web Wake browser extension submits each message reminder at most once; browser submit is NOT MCP ACK. There is no automatic wake of cloud inference when Web Chats are offline. inbox/sent/get inspect messages, ACK after actual reading, reply with evidence, untracked resolve or tracked verify only after checking work. Before completing a Web Main/Sub task and ending the turn, check your own web_mail(action=inbox) once more, handle newly received authorized actionable messages and truly ACK/reply; if blocked, state the blocker and next Owner/trigger without fake completion or endless polling. Private claimKey must not appear in mail or logs. Avoid duplicate Sol wake requests.`,
});
